How a head is copied: `auto` copies a snapshot of the heads whose storage takes
them, a zfs dataset, a btrfs subvolume or an LVM thin volume, taken while the
resources of the object are quiesced, which resume once the snapshots are
taken; `none` copies the heads themselves, the resources quiesced for the
whole copy.

A snapshot failing aborts the run, rather than copy the head under a quiesce
held for the whole copy.
